= Computer network — Simple =

A '''computer network''' connects computers and other devices so they can exchange data.

Devices communicate using agreed rules called protocols.

Networks can use Ethernet cables, fiber, Wi-Fi, cellular radio, or other links.

The Internet is a very large network of networks, but it is not the only kind of computer network.

A network lets computers communicate.

A distributed system goes further and coordinates several networked computers so they act together as part of one service or computation.

